# C2 orthogonal MC: SO(2N) and SO(2N+1) Haar 2nd moments of |Lambda'(1)|^2
# Hughes/Conrey-Rubinstein-Snaith literature constants of interest:
#   2/3   = 0.666667
#   1/12  = 0.083333  (CUE unitary G(3)^2/G(5))
#   1/18  = 0.055556  (1/12 * 16/24)
# For SO(2N): |Lambda'(1)|^2 = N^2 * Lambda(1)^2 (exact)
# For SO(2N+1): |Lambda'(1)|^2 = (prod_j 4 sin^2(theta_j/2))^2

================================================================================
SO(2N) Haar:  E[Lambda_A(1)^2]  and derived  E|Lambda'(1)|^2 / N^2 = same
================================================================================
N= 50 K=10000 skipped=  0 dt=33.1s
  log_max_seen = +13.568  (samples are heavy-tailed if log_max large)
  mean(log L^2) = -4.5712  std(log L^2) = 5.9208
  E[Lambda(1)^2] = 2.646665e+02  +/-  1.051e+02
     vs 2/3 = 0.6667 : ratio = 396.9997
     vs 1/12 = 0.0833: ratio = 3175.9979
     vs 1/18 = 0.0556: ratio = 4763.9968
